1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,170
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:02,240
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:03,310
(Generative AI technology was used
in some scenes.)

4
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,110
All right.

5
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,610
If you keep your promise first,
I will keep mine.

6
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,750
I said I understand.
Please just leave now.

7
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,280
I am terrified someone might see us.

8
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,790
Dae Chi, who is this?

9
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,760
Mom.

10
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:24,530
You...

11
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:25,860
You little brat!

12
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,700
Mom, what are you imagining
right now?

13
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:31,900
It is absolutely nothing like that.

14
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,710
What do you think I am imagining?

15
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,240
Go ahead and tell me.

16
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,140
I asked what it is.

17
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,480
No...

18
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:43,180
Mom.

19
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,450
Hello.

20
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,660
Yes, hello.

21
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:54,160
But who are you?

22
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,560
How do you know my son?

23
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,730
Well, as for who I am...

24
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:03,900
She is just a woman I know.

25
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:07,310
A woman you know?

26
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:15,350
Yes, that is correct.
I am just a woman he knows.

27
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,050
I will be on my way now.

28
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,050
- Goodbye.
- Yes.

29
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:22,990
Goodbye, young lady.

30
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,410
He said he just knows her.

31
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:42,670
It is nothing serious,
so let us go inside first.

32
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:44,310
Do you actually believe that?

33
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,880
Why would a mere acquaintance
come all the way to his house?

34
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:50,480
She is not a stranger,
so she can visit.

35
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:53,920
- Go inside.
- Why are you so strong?

36
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:55,650
Goodness.

37
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:06,200
You, stay right there.

38
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:13,340
Why?

39
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:16,270
I told you she is just
a woman I know.

40
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,340
Who are you trying to fool?

41
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,880
She is your girlfriend, right?
How long have you been seeing her?

42
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,180
Dae Chi.

43
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,620
Is this really the time
for you to be dating?

44
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,450
She looks much younger than you...

45
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,320
and seems to come
from a wealthy family.

46
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:35,430
I always hoped you'd date
and get married someday,

47
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:37,600
but things are different now.

48
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:40,600
Get your own life in order first...

49
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:41,730
before you start dating.

50
00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:44,570
I told you we are not dating!

51
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:46,770
And...

52
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:52,280
I know my situation
better than anyone.

53
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,410
You're worrying over nothing.

54
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:57,580
Dae Chi.

55
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:01,190
Son.

56
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,490
What is it now?

57
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:09,060
I'll help you carry your burden.

58
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:11,760
So don't worry.

59
00:03:13,770 --> 00:03:16,600
Are you eating well at work
and sleeping at night?

60
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:20,710
After causing a mess this bad,

61
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:24,510
if I could eat and sleep soundly,

62
00:03:27,550 --> 00:03:28,780
would I even be human?

63
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:42,860
But to me, Dae Chi...

64
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:47,500
has been my greatest pride
ever since he was in school.

65
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,570
My most dependable child.

66
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:00,180
(Always a Good Friend, Smiling Toys)

67
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:12,860
Why do you keep following me?

68
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,590
Excuse me?

69
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,030
I am just heading to the bus too.

70
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:47,060
(Onjeong Market)

71
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:49,690
(Always a Good Friend, Smiling Toys)

72
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:03,170
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

73
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:04,510
What is it?

74
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:07,910
About that cotton candy
from earlier.

75
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:10,980
Did it really taste that bad?

76
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:13,350
Actually...

77
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:17,890
(Blue Sky Orthopedics)

78
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:21,230
Actually, it was really delicious.

79
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:25,160
I paid for it, but thank you
for suggesting I try it.

80
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,770
All my life, I wanted...

81
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:31,040
to try cotton candy at least once.

82
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:34,670
I'm leaving!

83
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:57,430
She thanked me and said it tasted
good, so why did her face...

84
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,260
suddenly turn gloomy?

85
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,070
A taxi is coming.

86
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:16,510
- I am home.
- Welcome back, Seung Yun.

87
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:18,020
Have you eaten?

88
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,920
I ate plenty of good food
while I was out, Mrs. Anseong.

89
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,390
You do not need to prepare
anything for me.

90
00:06:23,450 --> 00:06:24,720
Seung Yun, you are here.

91
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:27,460
Yes, Uncle.

92
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:31,230
I guess Aunt hasn't left work yet.

93
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,800
What is that?

94
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,570
Do not even ask.

95
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:38,170
Your aunt went to meet
an investor today...

96
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,000
but fell before they could
even exchange greetings,

97
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,770
injuring her ankle.

98
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:43,570
So I am going to apply
a cold compress.

99
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,080
She went to bed early.

100
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:50,310
- Is she badly hurt?
- It is just a sprain.

101
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,890
I was so shocked that I ran over.

102
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,550
You must be tired
from your first day of work.

103
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:59,260
- Go and get some rest.
- Yes.

104
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:05,400
Dr. Ju came and set her ankle,

105
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,660
so she is fine now.

106
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:10,300
His bone-setting skills
are truly remarkable.

107
00:07:11,370 --> 00:07:12,970
Dr. Ju?

108
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:15,310
Yes, are you surprised
too, Seung Yun?

109
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:18,040
Imagine how surprised
I was watching him.

110
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:23,050
How is Grandma doing today?

111
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:26,950
The elder is in a sunny mood today.

112
00:07:28,650 --> 00:07:31,160
- What a relief.
- Let me take that.

113
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:45,940
- Grow up beautifully.
- Grandma, I am home.

114
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:51,110
<i>Love, love, my love</i>

115
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:56,480
<i>Love, love, love, my love</i>

116
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:05,520
Grandma, are you singing
to the money tree?

117
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:08,230
- Yes.
- What song is it?

118
00:08:09,330 --> 00:08:12,360
The love song from Chunhyangjeon.

119
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:18,670
Trees and flowers,
they are no different from people.

120
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,340
If you keep looking at them...

121
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:24,280
and tell them how pretty they are,

122
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:27,140
they can feel that love...

123
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:29,010
and use its strength...

124
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:31,120
to grow tall and strong.

125
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,050
Yes.

126
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,690
My eldest grandson,

127
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:42,560
when did you become
such a handsome young man?

128
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:44,960
Goodness.

129
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,170
Seung Yun.

130
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:53,340
- Yes, Grandma.
- Your late father and mother...

131
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:57,740
were so happy when you were born.

132
00:08:58,010 --> 00:08:59,310
From when you were a baby...

133
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:02,410
until they left this world together,

134
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:06,150
they treasured and loved you.

135
00:09:07,450 --> 00:09:11,160
Grandma remembers it all.

136
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,020
You, too...

137
00:09:13,930 --> 00:09:15,760
must never forget that.

138
00:09:16,190 --> 00:09:18,330
Yes, I always remember it too.

139
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:23,600
- I have never forgotten.
- If life ever...

140
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:27,070
hits you with crashing waves,

141
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:29,970
when you are in such pain...

142
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,410
that you feel shattered to pieces,

143
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:34,550
remember that love even more...

144
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:38,120
and find the strength to endure.

145
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:41,120
- Okay?
- Yes.

146
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:43,090
I will keep that in mind, Grandma.

147
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:44,890
Good.

148
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,220
Yes.

149
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,730
My poor child.

150
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,700
If only his parents
had not passed away so early,

151
00:09:54,930 --> 00:09:57,300
he would not have been so lonely...

152
00:09:57,370 --> 00:09:58,370
in a foreign land so far away,

153
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:01,610
growing up on his own.

154
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:03,870
Yes.

155
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,880
Grow up to be an even greater man.

156
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,350
Keep moving forward.

157
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:11,480
As long as your Grandma is alive,

158
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,620
I will protect you...

159
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:15,720
and not let a hair on your head
be harmed.

160
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,970
I even practiced what to say
before going to see her.

161
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:36,040
But of all days,
she took a day off today.

162
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:40,180
I could just find out
her contact information,

163
00:10:41,010 --> 00:10:43,210
but calling her personally
to say it is a bit...

164
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,120
too much.

165
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,260
Seung Yun.

166
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:54,830
When did you get here?

167
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:56,590
What?

168
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,100
- I got here a little while ago.
- I see.

169
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,270
I heard your mother fell down today?

170
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:04,640
Yes, I got a call and was surprised.

171
00:11:09,570 --> 00:11:10,570
Ta-da.

172
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:11,580
(DIY Mini Car)

173
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,580
What is this? Is it for me?

174
00:11:15,010 --> 00:11:16,610
Are you curious? Take it out.

175
00:11:23,090 --> 00:11:24,090
Why a mini car?

176
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:28,490
It is a gift. You look a bit down,

177
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,160
so I thought we could take
a trip down memory lane together.

178
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:32,060
You know the table
in the upstairs living room?

179
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:34,170
Clear it off and lay out a track.
That would be perfect.

180
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:36,400
What do you say? Do Yun,
you used to love...

181
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:38,170
playing with mini cars with me
more than anything.

182
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:39,940
I did?

183
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:41,940
Did I?

184
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:43,770
But...

185
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,680
I have a lot of work
to do right now.

186
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:49,980
Really?

187
00:11:50,850 --> 00:11:52,380
Then we can just do it next time.

188
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:54,750
Get back to work.

189
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,090
Okay.

190
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:23,950
(DIY Mini Car)

191
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:43,900
I owe her a huge thank-you for this.

192
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:56,380
(This design... 100 percent cotton
rather than linen...)

193
00:12:58,950 --> 00:12:59,950
(Preppy Look? Balletcore?
Campus Casual?)

194
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,090
(Soft Monotone? Sporty Feminine?)

195
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:08,230
Should I give this to her or not?

196
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:30,080
Your designs, Kang Da Mi,
only have ideas about the clothes,

197
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:31,550
but they lack an understanding...

198
00:13:31,550 --> 00:13:33,420
of the people
who will actually wear them.

199
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:39,960
Well, it is not like he knows
everything about people either.

200
00:13:42,490 --> 00:13:44,560
But he is not exactly wrong.

201
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:49,170
Even if we do not get along,

202
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:51,070
if I can learn something from him,

203
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,640
I should admit it and learn.
That would help me grow.

204
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:57,210
I want to ask him more.

205
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:59,880
I have so many things I want to ask.

206
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:07,590
Wait, but where on earth
did my wallet go?

207
00:14:07,850 --> 00:14:09,020
It could not have just
grown legs and walked away.

208
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:10,450
I cannot find it anywhere.

209
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:29,970
Da Mi.

210
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:33,080
Are you awake, sweetie?

211
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,180
Did you sleep well?

212
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:41,790
You are already ready for work.

213
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,890
Come downstairs and eat breakfast.

214
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,760
I made your favorite japchae.

215
00:14:51,130 --> 00:14:52,900
Mom, what is wrong with you?

216
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:56,100
What do you mean?

217
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:59,570
Why are you suddenly acting
so out of character?

218
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:08,210
My daughter must be exhausted
from working so hard...

219
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:10,580
Oh, my.

220
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,620
You shed your clothes
like a snake sheds its skin.

221
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,960
Sweetie, I packed you lunch, too.

222
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:22,890
You like cherry tomatoes, right?

223
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:27,000
Eat those as a snack.
And apple mangoes...

224
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,570
I'll buy some for you today.

225
00:15:29,730 --> 00:15:31,040
You can have them tonight
when you get home.

226
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:33,470
Mom.

227
00:15:35,310 --> 00:15:36,340
Yes?

228
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,280
If you have something to say to me,
just say it.

229
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:42,250
Just be direct with me.
This is so unlike you.

230
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,120
Da Mi,

231
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:48,290
the money I saved
for your wedding...

232
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,590
I think I need to use it...

233
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:58,760
for Dae Chi first.

234
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,900
I told you to just be
upfront with me.

235
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,470
What?

236
00:16:06,970 --> 00:16:08,410
What are you talking about?

237
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,740
Come downstairs
and eat your breakfast.

238
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,480
This is so annoying.

239
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,630
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

240
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,360
So,

241
00:16:33,530 --> 00:16:35,270
when did you reschedule
the meeting for?

242
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:39,870
They must be desperate.
They want to meet today.

243
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,640
I acted busy, just like you said.

244
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,080
Wow.

245
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,680
- Good job.
- We have little time...

246
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,010
before the investment arrives.

247
00:16:49,450 --> 00:16:52,620
- Can you find a weakness?
- Everyone has a weakness.

248
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,220
Do not worry
and just focus on the meeting.

249
00:16:57,090 --> 00:16:58,090
Got it.

250
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:04,060
Got it. He speaks Korean well, too.

251
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:15,510
Why does he only solve
the yellow side?

252
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:26,780
I, Jo Ri Ja,

253
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:28,690
have gone by the name Mona Lisa...

254
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:30,150
for so many years.

255
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:31,690
But if I have mastered one thing,

256
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,390
it is drawing eyebrows.

257
00:17:44,330 --> 00:17:45,340
Mother,

258
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:47,810
I made spicy noodles
for the first time in a while,

259
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:50,770
and the sauce turned out great.
Should I set the table for you now?

260
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:52,610
I told you I have no appetite.

261
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,680
You go ahead and eat
a whole bowl yourself.

262
00:17:57,750 --> 00:17:59,780
Are you feeling uncomfortable
anywhere else?

263
00:18:01,990 --> 00:18:04,460
Should I make you something else
instead of noodles?

264
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:08,760
The pickled melon in the jar
has fermented beautifully.

265
00:18:09,190 --> 00:18:11,360
It is deliciously crisp and chewy.

266
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,060
Would you like to try some
to get your appetite back?

267
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,430
I said no.

268
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,870
You are being quite annoying again.

269
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,350
I'd rather...

270
00:18:28,910 --> 00:18:30,610
you just say,
"You raised your son wrong."

271
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:31,880
"This is all your fault
as his mother."

272
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:33,250
Just scold me, Mother.

273
00:18:35,790 --> 00:18:38,560
The children make trouble below,
and the elders scold me above.

274
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:40,920
I'm always stuck in the middle.

275
00:18:58,110 --> 00:19:00,380
Grandma seems sick,

276
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,310
and Mom...

277
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:08,550
Do I really have to make
chicken soup myself?

278
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,420
Me, Kang Gang Nam?

279
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,690
No way.

280
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,860
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

281
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:27,040
As expected.

282
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,140
Just look at Dr. Ju's
taste in rice cakes.

283
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:32,210
Such refined taste and style.

284
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,250
He must be very tidy, too.

285
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,650
But...

286
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,550
why is no one here?

287
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,130
(Consultation Room)

288
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,600
Oh my.

289
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:00,600
I guess I like men in white coats.

290
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:04,780
Hello. Are you here for a checkup?

291
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:11,110
Yes, I am not feeling very well.

292
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,790
Our staff member
is not here right now.

293
00:20:14,950 --> 00:20:16,890
I will help you register
in a moment,

294
00:20:16,950 --> 00:20:18,260
so please come in first.

295
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,990
Yes, Dr. Ju.

296
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,400
What seems to be the problem?

297
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,770
Well, you see, Dr. Ju...

298
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,810
I have not been
sleeping well lately.

299
00:20:34,970 --> 00:20:39,540
My heart races, then calms down,

300
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:42,910
and my mind keeps wandering.

301
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:46,380
Getting older makes me wonder
what the point of life even is.

302
00:20:46,450 --> 00:20:48,120
And all this endless work...

303
00:20:48,990 --> 00:20:51,320
I am sorry.

304
00:20:51,390 --> 00:20:53,160
(Dr. Ju Kyung Ho)

305
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:57,660
I just wonder what good it does
to work so hard.

306
00:20:58,460 --> 00:20:59,960
Excuse me, Dr. Ju.

307
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:04,570
What kind of medicine should I take
to get better?

308
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,370
Could you perhaps...

309
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:10,110
start with a hands-on exam?

310
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:12,340
Or,

311
00:21:12,410 --> 00:21:15,010
should I lie down
on that bed over there?

312
00:21:15,250 --> 00:21:18,020
Actually, I have been getting
indigestion a lot lately,

313
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:20,480
and my stomach has been upset.

314
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:24,590
Well...

315
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:26,520
Yes, Dr. Ju.

316
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:29,830
I hesitate to say this, but...

317
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:33,530
Dr. Ju, you can speak freely.

318
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:35,570
We're already this close.

319
00:21:35,630 --> 00:21:37,530
Why are you hesitating?

320
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:42,570
Let me write you a referral.

321
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:44,780
You should see a gynecologist...

322
00:21:44,910 --> 00:21:45,980
as soon as possible.

323
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:49,050
What? A gynecologist...

324
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:54,150
- Why would I go there?
- Your symptoms...

325
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:57,020
may be signs of early menopause.

326
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:59,160
I know you are busy,

327
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,320
but please go as soon as possible.

328
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,360
Your health is more important
than work.

329
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:06,100
Menopause...

330
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:08,400
(Consultation Room)

331
00:22:09,430 --> 00:22:10,600
I am going through menopause?

332
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,400
(Consultation Room)

333
00:22:18,210 --> 00:22:19,210
Okay.

334
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,840
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

335
00:22:20,910 --> 00:22:22,910
(Consultation Room)

336
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:24,550
That woman? Goodness!

337
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,490
What do I do? What should I do?

338
00:22:29,990 --> 00:22:31,350
(Nursing Assistant Park Ji Young)

339
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,400
It hurts.

340
00:22:51,070 --> 00:22:53,180
I ended up bleeding after all.

341
00:22:58,950 --> 00:23:00,050
Ye Ri.

342
00:23:00,850 --> 00:23:01,850
My daughter.

343
00:23:03,450 --> 00:23:05,960
How did your mother
end up like this?

344
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:09,630
It hurts.

345
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:14,260
It hurts.

346
00:23:35,090 --> 00:23:36,190
(Resident Registration Card,
Kang Da Mi)

347
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:38,020
She has grown into a lovely woman.

348
00:23:39,390 --> 00:23:41,290
I wonder if she even remembers me.

349
00:23:42,930 --> 00:23:46,000
Even if she remembers me,
would she have any fond memories?

350
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:48,400
She must be full of resentment.

351
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Goodness.

352
00:23:53,370 --> 00:23:55,770
- My knee.
- Goodness.

353
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:04,080
Even if you are on your break,

354
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:05,650
should you not change
out of your uniform...

355
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,150
before walking around?

356
00:24:07,650 --> 00:24:09,120
That is not what is important
right now.

357
00:24:09,190 --> 00:24:12,520
- This is an emergency.
- What on earth is going on...

358
00:24:12,590 --> 00:24:13,790
for you to make such a fuss?

359
00:24:14,090 --> 00:24:15,090
Ri Ja.

360
00:24:15,290 --> 00:24:19,230
- I saw Ri Ja at the hospital.
- Ri Ja? Jo Ri Ja?

361
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,970
- You mean you saw my sister-in-law?
- I am telling you.

362
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:26,270
Your ex-wife's sister, Jo Ri Ja...

363
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:28,040
came to my hospital as a patient!

364
00:24:31,210 --> 00:24:33,910
I thought you said
you were confident.

365
00:24:34,010 --> 00:24:36,910
- You were going to face her.
- Honey.

366
00:24:38,650 --> 00:24:41,050
So you ran off
the moment you saw her.

367
00:24:41,650 --> 00:24:42,850
Right?

368
00:24:42,950 --> 00:24:44,920
Only the guilty feel so uneasy...

369
00:24:45,790 --> 00:24:47,590
which shows you have a conscience.

370
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:50,190
Just put on your ointment.

371
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:52,730
You are an accomplice too,
what is wrong with you?

372
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:54,660
Wait.

373
00:24:55,630 --> 00:24:56,700
Your sister-in-law?

374
00:24:58,030 --> 00:25:00,300
Are you saying Jo Ri Ja is
still your sister-in-law?

375
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:08,010
Are you saying Summit Investment
responded to our contact?

376
00:25:08,250 --> 00:25:09,280
Yes, CEO Jeon.

377
00:25:09,580 --> 00:25:11,720
At first, they claimed
their schedule was full,

378
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:13,380
but sent a time and place.

379
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:15,520
That is a relief.

380
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:17,550
And CEO Jeon,

381
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:20,290
your new heel broke...

382
00:25:20,390 --> 00:25:22,360
at that important meeting.

383
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:24,360
You should file a complaint...

384
00:25:24,430 --> 00:25:26,130
directly with the department store.

385
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:31,530
How could they make a VVIP like you
experience such a disaster?

386
00:25:31,900 --> 00:25:33,070
So, Assistant Manager Kang,

387
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:35,610
are you telling a CEO like me...

388
00:25:35,710 --> 00:25:37,770
to complain to the store myself?

389
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,240
Excuse me?

390
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:42,010
I apologize, CEO Jeon.

391
00:25:42,710 --> 00:25:45,680
Then should I go to the store myself
and make a complaint?

392
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:50,090
You should know what I want...

393
00:25:50,150 --> 00:25:51,990
better than anyone here by now.

394
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:54,960
Handle it yourself.

395
00:25:57,530 --> 00:26:00,260
Yes, CEO Jeon.
I will handle it myself.

396
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:08,870
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

397
00:26:08,970 --> 00:26:10,670
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

398
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:11,740
Right.

399
00:26:12,510 --> 00:26:13,940
If you are my marble,

400
00:26:14,580 --> 00:26:16,210
then roll like one.

401
00:26:18,550 --> 00:26:20,550
(Product Planning Department)

402
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:26,820
CEO Jeon told me
that I am her person now.

403
00:26:28,930 --> 00:26:30,860
Should I show them who is boss...

404
00:26:31,290 --> 00:26:33,960
so they cannot say a word?

405
00:26:36,630 --> 00:26:38,440
Yes, I should show them.

406
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:43,340
We met our sales target early today,

407
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,840
and all the customers
were nice, right, Da Mi?

408
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:47,540
I know.

409
00:26:47,780 --> 00:26:50,950
I suppose we need to have
a peaceful day at least once.

410
00:26:54,750 --> 00:26:56,050
Welcome, ma'am.

411
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:58,990
I do not think we have met before.
Do you have a reservation?

412
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:03,390
- Are you the manager here?
- Yes, I am Manager Kang Da Mi.

413
00:27:03,890 --> 00:27:06,460
It is a pleasure to meet you.
How may I help...

414
00:27:08,330 --> 00:27:09,330
Da Mi.

415
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:14,340
What is the meaning of this, ma'am?

416
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:15,970
(K Department Store)

417
00:27:16,540 --> 00:27:17,570
Pick it up.

418
00:27:18,010 --> 00:27:20,310
- Excuse me?
- Pick it up and see...

419
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,480
for yourself.

420
00:27:24,710 --> 00:27:26,280
You pick it up, ma'am.

421
00:27:27,650 --> 00:27:28,650
What?

422
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:31,550
You heard me.
I said the person who threw it...

423
00:27:31,690 --> 00:27:34,690
- should pick it up.
- You asked what I meant.

424
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:37,760
If you are curious, pick it up
and see for yourself.

425
00:27:37,930 --> 00:27:39,900
This is the department store's
VIP boutique.

426
00:27:40,300 --> 00:27:42,030
It is not your personal shoe closet.

427
00:27:53,140 --> 00:27:55,080
(Mission: Mompossible)

428
00:28:15,030 --> 00:28:16,770
She is just
a department store employee.

429
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:19,800
- How could she be so shameless?
- What does being...

430
00:28:19,870 --> 00:28:20,900
a store employee have to do with it?

431
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:23,540
That woman who just left,
she was causing a scene, right?

432
00:28:23,610 --> 00:28:27,710
- What happened exactly?
- What a fool.

433
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:31,780
- Yes, Mother.
- You are fired as of this moment.

434
00:28:32,420 --> 00:28:34,420
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
